      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8c4dd330",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image shows a tiger lying down with a defeated or dejected expression, juxtaposed with the text 'when you lose your first boxing match.' The overall intent is to humorously convey the feeling of disappointment or embarrassment after a first loss, using the tiger as a metaphor for a powerful or intimidating figure who has been unexpectedly defeated. The meme is not inherently toxic, abusive, or hateful as it does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics. It is a lighthearted, self-deprecating joke that relies on the contrast between the tiger's natural dominance and its apparent defeat. There is no evidence of cyberbullying, misogyny, ableism, or other forms of toxicity. The intent is to evoke relatability and humor through analogical mapping: the tiger represents a formidable opponent or person who is unexpectedly defeated, mirroring the human experience of losing a first significant challenge.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ff951ca9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
